---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SectionHead from '../components/SectionHead.astro';
import { site, timeline, languages, certifications, teaching } from '../lib/site';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Milad Poshtdari — Go and systems engineer in Hamburg, IT consultant at Lufthansa Industry Solutions."
  context="ABOUT"
>
  <section class="panel">
    <span class="lbl">About</span>
    <h1 class="display" style="font-size:clamp(30px,5vw,52px)">Who I am</h1>
    <div class="rule-y"></div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        I build and improve services: large-scale web applications and enterprise systems, the
        kind that have to keep working while nobody is watching. Today that happens as an IT
        consultant at <strong>{site.company}</strong> in {site.location} — where the systems are
        real, the constraints are real, and the deadlines belong to someone else.
      </p>
      <p>
        Before Hamburg there was Tehran, and a backend developer who kept wanting to know what
        the standard library was actually doing. That question never went away. It is why I write
        C for fun, why I read the Go scheduler instead of only using it, and why I went back to
        university at Universität zu Lübeck while working full time.
      </p>
      <blockquote>{site.motto}</blockquote>
      <p>
        That line on my GitHub profile is not anti-tooling. It is a preference for understanding
        the thing I am shipping. Tools that make me faster are welcome. Tools that make me faster
        at producing code I could not explain are not.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="grid g-side mt">
    <section class="panel">
      <SectionHead title="Trajectory" />
      {
        timeline.map((item) => (
          <div class="tl">
            <span class="tl-year mono">{item.year}</span>
            <div>
              <div class="tl-title">{item.title}</div>
              <div class="mute" style="font-size:14px">
                {item.detail}
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </section>

    <div class="stack-gap">
      <section class="panel">
        <SectionHead title="Languages" />
        {
          languages.map((l) => (
            <div class="lg">
              <span class="k">{l.level}</span>
              <span>
                {l.name} <span class="mute">· {l.native}</span>
              </span>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </section>

      <section class="panel">
        <SectionHead title="Certifications" count={`${certifications.length}`} />
        <div class="chips">
          {certifications.map((c) => <span class="chip" title={c.issuer}>{c.name}</span>)}
        </div>
        <p class="mute" style="font-size:12px;margin-top:10px">
          Ardan Labs for the Go, Docker, and Kubernetes track.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="panel mt">
    <SectionHead title={teaching.headline} />
    <div class="prose">
      {teaching.body.map((line) => <p>{line}</p>)}
      <p>
        Teaching is the fastest way to find the holes in your own understanding. It is also the
        reason I care about documentation in languages other than English: the barrier to entry in
        this field is often linguistic before it is technical.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="panel panel-dark mt">
    <span class="lbl">Next</span>
    <h2 style="font-size:22px;font-weight:600;margin:8px 0 6px">Where this is going</h2>
    <p style="max-width:60ch">
      Deeper into compilers and runtime internals, and further into the systems layer generally.
      The long-term interest is the same one that started it: understanding the machine all the
      way down.
    </p>
    <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:16px">
      <a class="btn btn-solid" href="/now/">What I'm doing now →</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .tl {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 108px 1fr;
    gap: 14px;
    padding: 12px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .tl:last-child {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }
  .tl-year {
    font-size: 11.5px;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--yellow-deep);
    font-weight: 700;
    padding-top: 3px;
  }
  .tl-title {
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  @media (max-width: 620px) {
    .tl {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 2px;
    }
  }
</style>
